            "exam_source": "NEET PG 2024 Recall",
            "topic": "Gastrointestinal Surgery - Courvoisier Law & Whipple",
            "question": "A 62-year-old male presents with deep progressive jaundice, dark urine, pale stools, significant pruritus, and a 12 kg weight loss. Physical examination reveals a palpable, non-tender, smooth gallbladder in the right upper quadrant (Courvoisier's sign). Contrast CT demonstrates a 3 cm adenocarcinoma in the head of the pancreas causing the 'double-duct sign'. What is the definitive oncological resection of choice?",
            "options": {
              "A": "Pancreaticoduodenectomy (Whipple Procedure)",
              "B": "Distal Pancreatectomy with Splenectomy",
              "C": "Total Gastrectomy with Roux-en-Y reconstruction",
              "D": "Cholecystojejunostomy alone"
            },
            "correct_option": "A",
            "explanation": {
              "rationale": "Courvoisier's Law states that in a patient with progressive obstructive jaundice, a palpable, enlarged, non-tender gallbladder indicates an obstructive lesion distal to the cystic duct that is NOT a gallstone (most commonly carcinoma of the head of the pancreas, periampullary carcinoma, or distal cholangiocarcinoma), because chronic gallstone cholecystitis leads to a fibrotic, shrunken, non-distensible gallbladder wall. The 'Double-Duct Sign' on CT/MRCP confirms simultaneous obstruction and dilation of both the CBD and Main Pancreatic Duct. The definitive curative surgical operation for resectable adenocarcinoma of the pancreatic head is PANCREATICODUODENECTOMY (WHIPPLE PROCEDURE), which resects the pancreatic head/uncinate, duodenum, proximal jejunum, distal CBD, gallbladder, and antrum.",
              "distractor_analysis": {
                "B": "Distal Pancreatectomy with Splenectomy is performed for tumors located in the pancreatic BODY and TAIL.",
                "C": "Total gastrectomy is indicated for gastric adenocarcinoma.",
                "D": "Cholecystojejunostomy is purely palliative biliary bypass, not an oncological cure."
              },
              "high_yield_pearl": "Courvoisier's Law: Jaundice + Palpable non-tender gallbladder = Malignant obstruction of pancreatic head / periampullary region (NOT gallstones!). Surgical cure = Whipple Procedure (Pancreaticoduodenectomy). Double-duct sign = Dilated CBD + Dilated Pancreatic Duct."
            },
