            "question": "A 52-year-old male with a 20-year history of chronic duodenal ulcer presents with persistent, projectile, non-bilious vomiting containing food particles eaten 24 hours earlier, succussion splash audible in the epigastrium, and profound dehydration. What is the classic electrolyte and acid-base derangement in Gastric Outlet Obstruction (GOO), and why does 'Paradoxical Aciduria' develop?",
