            "question": "A 58-year-old male presents with vague epigastric fullness and occult gastrointestinal bleeding. Contrast CT shows a 7 cm well-circumscribed, submucosal, exophytic mass arising from the gastric fundus with central necrosis. Histopathology reveals fascicles of spindle cells that stain strongly positive for CD117 (c-KIT) and DOG-1. What molecular driver mutation causes GIST, and what targeted tyrosine kinase inhibitor is used for adjuvant therapy?",
