            "question": "A 38-year-old male presents with intermittent purulent and serosanguinous discharge from an external opening in the perianal skin. Goodsall's rule predicts the anatomical trajectory of the fistulous tract based on an imaginary transverse line drawn through the center of the anus. According to Goodsall's Rule, what is the path of an external opening located ANTERIOR vs POSTERIOR to the transverse line?",
