              "rationale": "Sentinel Lymph Node (SLN) Concept (Cabanas): The Sentinel Node is the first hypothetical lymph node in the regional lymphatic basin that receives afferent lymphatic drainage directly from the primary tumor. If the sentinel node is negative for metastasis, all downstream nodes are negative (> 98% accuracy), sparing the patient from the morbidities of Axillary Lymph Node Dissection (ALND: chronic upper extremity lymphedema, winged scapula from long thoracic nerve injury, sensory loss from intercostobrachial nerve injury). Dual-Tracer Mapping Technique: Injection of: (1) Radioactive Technetium-99m Sulfur Colloid (detected intraoperatively with a handheld gamma probe - 'hot node'), and (2) Blue Dye (Isosulfan Blue, Patent Blue V, or Methylene Blue - visually stains afferent lymphatics and nodes bright blue - 'blue node'). Any node that is 'hot' (>= 10% of the ex-vivo count of the hottest node), 'blue', or clinically suspicious on palpation is excised as a sentinel node. ACOSOG Z0011 Trial Paradigm Shift: In patients with T1-T2 breast cancer undergoing Breast-Conserving Surgery (BCS) with 1 or 2 positive sentinel nodes, COMPLETION AXILLARY LYMPH NODE DISSECTION (ALND) CAN BE SAFELY OMITTED without compromising disease-free or overall survival, provided patients receive standard tangential whole-breast radiation therapy and adjuvant systemic therapy (chemo/endocrine).",
