              "rationale": "Medullary Thyroid Carcinoma (MTC) accounts for 3-5% of all thyroid cancers. Origin: PARAFOLLICULAR C-CELLS (neuroendocrine cells of neural crest origin located in the upper 1/3 of thyroid lobes, derived from the Ultimobranchial Body). C-cells synthesize and secrete CALCITONIN (the pathognomonic serum biomarker for MTC; doubling time < 6 months indicates aggressive recurrence). CEA (Carcinoembryonic Antigen) is also secreted and serves as an important prognostic marker. Histopathology Hallmark: Nests of polygonal / spindle neuroendocrine cells embedded in an abundant acellular AMYLOID STROMA (composed of polymerized pro-calcitonin fibrils, staining bright orange-red with Congo Red and demonstrating pathognomonic APPLE-GREEN BIREFRINGENCE under polarized light!). Genetics: ~75% sporadic; ~25% familial as part of MEN 2A or MEN 2B or Familial MTC (FMTC), driven by germline gain-of-function mutations in the RET PROTO-ONCOGENE on Chromosome 10q11. MANDATORY PREOPERATIVE SAFETY RULE: In ANY patient diagnosed with Medullary Thyroid Carcinoma, ONE MUST SCREEN FOR CONCOMITANT PHEOCHROMOCYTOMA (Plasma Free Metanephrines or 24-hr urinary metanephrines) BEFORE SCHEDULING THYROID SURGERY! If pheochromocytoma is present, the pheochromocytoma MUST BE RESECTED FIRST to prevent fatal intraoperative hypertensive crisis during thyroidectomy! Surgical standard: Total Thyroidectomy with Central Compartment (Level VI) Neck Dissection.",
