            "question": "A 24-year-old primigravida at 34 weeks of gestation presents with severe preeclampsia (BP 170/110 mmHg, 3+ proteinuria) and suddenly develops a generalized tonic-clonic convulsion. Magnesium Sulfate (MgSO4) is initiated according to the Zuspan regimen. Which clinical sign is the EARLIEST indicator of impending magnesium toxicity that mandates immediate discontinuation of the infusion?",
