            "topic": "Postpartum Hemorrhage - Uterotonic Selection & Contraindications",
            "question": "A 28-year-old female experiences severe primary postpartum hemorrhage (blood loss > 800 mL) due to uterine atony immediately following delivery. She has a documented past history of severe bronchial asthma. Which potent second-line uterotonic agent is STRICTLY CONTRAINDICATED in this patient due to the risk of precipitating lethal bronchospasm?",
            "options": {
              "A": "Carboprost tromethamine (15-methyl PGF2-alpha)",
              "B": "Methylergometrine (Methergine)",
              "C": "Misoprostol (PGE1 analogue)",
              "D": "Oxytocin"
            },
            "correct_option": "A",
            "explanation": {
              "rationale": "Carboprost tromethamine is an analogue of Prostaglandin F2-alpha (PGF2a) that produces powerful, sustained myometrial contractions to arrest atonic PPH. However, PGF2a also acts directly on airway smooth muscle prostanoid receptors to cause intense, life-threatening bronchoconstriction. Therefore, Carboprost is STRICTLY CONTRAINDICATED in patients with BRONCHIAL ASTHMA. In parallel, Methylergometrine causes intense peripheral vasoconstriction and is STRICTLY CONTRAINDICATED in patients with HYPERTENSION, PREECLAMPSIA, or cardiac disease.",
              "distractor_analysis": {
                "A": "Correct. Carboprost (PGF2a) causes severe bronchospasm and is contraindicated in asthma.",
                "B": "Methylergometrine is contraindicated in hypertension and preeclampsia, but not asthma.",
                "C": "Misoprostol (PGE1) causes bronchodilation and is safe in asthma.",
                "D": "Oxytocin is first-line and safe in asthma."
              },
              "high_yield_pearl": "Uterotonic Contraindications Rule: Carboprost (PGF2-alpha) -> CONTRAINDICATED in BRONCHIAL ASTHMA (causes bronchospasm). Methylergometrine (Methergine) -> CONTRAINDICATED in HYPERTENSION & PREECLAMPSIA (causes vasoconstrictive hypertensive crisis). Misoprostol (PGE1) -> Safe in asthma and hypertension."
            },
