            "question": "A 52-year-old multipara complains of involuntary loss of small amounts of urine whenever she coughs, sneezes, or laughs. Urinalysis is normal, and post-void residual volume is 25 mL (normal < 50). What type of urinary incontinence is this, and what is the first-line conservative management followed by the gold-standard surgical procedure?",
