            "topic": "Primary vs Secondary Dysmenorrhea",
            "question": "A 19-year-old nulligravida presents with severe cramping lower abdominal and suprapubic pain that begins 2 to 4 hours before the onset of menstrual flow and lasts for the first 24 to 48 hours. Pelvic examination is completely normal. What biochemical mediator is responsible, and what is the first-line pharmacotherapy?",
