            "question": "During resuscitation of a term infant born through meconium-stained amniotic fluid who is apneic and bradycardic (HR 50 bpm) despite 30 seconds of effective PPV via endotracheal tube with chest rise, what is the indicated next step under NRP 8th Edition?",
