              "rationale": "NRP 8th Edition Resuscitation Flow: (1) Initial Steps (within 30-60 seconds): Warm, dry, stimulate, clear airway if obstructed. In meconium-stained amniotic fluid: Routine endotracheal suctioning is NO LONGER RECOMMENDED; manage non-vigorous infant identically with gentle suction and immediate PPV; (2) Apnea / Gasping OR HR < 100 bpm: Start POSITIVE PRESSURE VENTILATION (PPV) immediately at 40-60 breaths/min. FiO2 = 21% for term (>= 35 wks), 21-30% for preterm (< 35 wks). Connect pulse oximeter and ECG; (3) If chest not moving with PPV: Execute 'MR. SOPA' corrective steps (Mask adjustment, Reposition airway, Suction mouth/nose, Open mouth, Pressure increase, Alternative airway [Endotracheal tube or Laryngeal Mask Airway]); (4) CHEST COMPRESSIONS INDICATIONS: Heart rate remains < 60 bpm despite at least 30 seconds of EFFECTIVE PPV that achieves chest movement (usually via endotracheal tube). Technique: 2-thumb encircling-hands technique on lower third of sternum (depth 1/3 anterior-posterior chest diameter). RATIO = 3 COMPRESSIONS TO 1 VENTILATION (3:1 ratio; 90 compressions + 30 breaths = 120 events/min). When compressions start, increase FiO2 to 100%! (5) Epinephrine: Indicated ONLY if HR remains < 60 bpm despite 60 seconds of coordinated compressions + effective PPV with 100% O2. Dose: IV/IO = 0.02 mg/kg (0.2 mL/kg of 1:10,000 solution) followed by 3 mL NS flush; Endotracheal = 0.1 mg/kg (less effective).",
