            "question": "A 36-hour-old term infant develops hypothermia (temperature 35.8 C), lethargy, poor feeding, tachypnea, and delayed capillary refill (4 seconds). Blood culture is pending. What are the most common pathogens causing Early-Onset Neonatal Sepsis (EOS), and what is the empirical antibiotic regimen of choice?",
