              "rationale": "Phototherapy for Neonatal Hyperbilirubinemia: Mechanism of Action: Light absorption by unconjugated bilirubin in cutaneous and subcutaneous capillary beds. Wavelength: BLUE-GREEN SPECTRUM (460 TO 490 nm - coincides with the peak absorption wavelength of bilirubin bound to albumin). Three Photochemical Reactions: (1) STRUCTURAL PHOTOISOMERIZATION (IRREVERSIBLE, 75-80% of effect - PRINCIPAL MECHANISM): Converts toxic 4Z,15Z-bilirubin into LUMIRUBIN (a structural isomer that is water-soluble and excreted rapidly in bile and urine WITHOUT requiring hepatic glucuronide conjugation!); (2) Configurational Isomerization (Reversible, 15-20%): Converts 4Z,15Z-bilirubin into 4Z,15E-bilirubin (reversible in bile); (3) Photo-Oxidation (minor < 5%): Degrades bilirubin into small polar colorless pyrroles. Adverse Effects and Complications: (1) BRONZE BABY SYNDROME: A grayish-brown discoloration of skin, serum, and urine occurring in neonates treated with phototherapy who have CONCOMITANT CHOLESTASIS / CONJUGATED HYPERBILIRUBINEMIA (due to photo-induced oxidation of accumulated copper porphyrins; completely benign, resolves after stopping phototherapy); (2) Insensible fluid loss (increased by 20-40%, requires 10-20% extra hydration); (3) Loose green watery stools (due to osmotic cathartic effect of photoproducts); (4) Retinal damage (EYES MUST BE SHIELDED with opaque eye patches!); (5) Erythematous macular rash, purpura, and hypocalcemia. Contraindication: CONGENITAL PORPHYRIA (phototherapy triggers severe bullous photodermatitis and death!).",
