            "topic": "Exchange Transfusion - Indications & Volumes",
            "question": "A full-term infant with severe Rh hemolytic disease has a total serum bilirubin of 26 mg/dL unresponsive to intensive phototherapy, with early lethargy and poor feeding. Double-volume exchange transfusion is planned. What is the calculated volume of blood required for an infant weighing 3.0 kg, and what type of blood is cross-matched?",
