            "question": "A very preterm infant born at 26 weeks gestation weighing 800 grams develops sudden pallor, acute drop in hematocrit, full bulging fontanelle, and apnea on day 2 of life. Cranial ultrasound demonstrates hemorrhage in the subependymal germinal matrix extending into the lateral ventricles, filling > 50% of the ventricular space with ventricular dilatation. What grade of IVH is this according to Papile's Classification?",
