            "question": "A 12-year-old child is evaluated for exertional leg fatigue and headaches. Blood pressure in the right upper arm is 150/90 mmHg, while blood pressure in the right calf is 90/60 mmHg. Femoral pulses are weak and delayed compared to radial pulses (Radio-femoral delay). Chest radiograph reveals bilateral inferior rib notching (Roesler's sign) and the 'Figure of 3' sign on the aortic knob. What congenital heart lesion is most frequently co-existent?",
