            "question": "A 7-year-old boy presents with smoky, cola-colored urine, puffy eyelids, oliguria, and a blood pressure of 145/95 mmHg 2 weeks after recovering from Streptococcal pharyngitis. Complement C3 is markedly decreased, while C4 is normal. Renal biopsy reveals diffuse endocapillary proliferative glomerulonephritis. What are the pathognomonic electron microscopic findings, and what is the typical clinical course?",
