            "question": "An 8-month-old previously thriving infant suddenly develops paroxysms of severe, inconsolable colicky abdominal pain accompanied by screaming and drawing up of the legs, alternating with periods of lethargy. On examination, a tubular 'Sausage-Shaped' mass is palpated in the right upper quadrant, the right lower quadrant feels empty (Dance's sign), and rectal examination reveals 'Red Currant Jelly' stools. What is the diagnostic imaging modality and initial treatment of choice?",
