            "question": "A 68-year-old postmenopausal female sustains a low-trauma fracture of the distal radius. Dual-Energy X-ray Absorptiometry (DEXA) of the femoral neck reveals a bone mineral density T-score of -2.8 SD. What WHO category defines this value, what is the first-line antiresorptive pharmacotherapy, and what is the mechanism of action?",
