              "rationale": "Osteopetrosis ('Marble Bone Disease' / Albers-Schonberg Disease): A rare genetic disorder characterized by generalized sclerosis of the entire skeleton caused by COMPLETE FAILURE OF OSTEOCLASTIC BONE RESORPTION. Pathophysiology: Osteoclasts cannot acidify the resorption pit / Howship's lacuna to dissolve mineralized bone matrix. Defective Genes: (1) TCIRG1 mutation (vacuolar H+-ATPase a3 subunit proton pump in 50% of infantile malignant cases); (2) CARBONIC ANHYDRASE II (CA II) DEFICIENCY (associated with autosomal recessive osteopetrosis, Renal Tubular Acidosis, and cerebral calcification); (3) CLCN7 (chloride channel 7). Forms: (a) Malignant Infantile Osteopetrosis (Autosomal Recessive: lethal without treatment): Dense unremodeled bone obliterate the medullary marrow cavities, causing PANCYTOPENIA and massive EXTRAMEDULLARY HEMATOPOIESIS in liver and spleen (profound Hepatosplenomegaly). Sclerosis narrows cranial nerve foramina, compressing CN II, VII, and VIII, resulting in BLINDNESS (optic atrophy), facial nerve palsy, and sensorineural deafness; (b) Autosomal Dominant Osteopetrosis (Albers-Schonberg / adult type: mild, incidental sclerosis or recurrent pathological fractures). Classic Radiographic Signs: (1) UNIVERSALLY DENSE, CHALK-WHITE 'MARBLE BONES' (loss of corticomedullary differentiation), (2) 'BONE-WITHIN-BONE' APPEARANCE (endobone in vertebrae and pelvis), (3) 'ERLENMEYER FLASK DEFORMITY' of distal femoral metaphyses, (4) 'Sandwich Vertebrae' (dense endplates resembling Rugger-Jersey spine). CURATIVE THERAPY FOR INFANTILE MALIGNANT DISEASE: ALLOGENEIC HEMATOPOIETIC STEM CELL TRANSPLANTATION (HSCT: because osteoclasts are derived from monocyte-macrophage hematopoietic stem cell precursors, marrow transplantation repopulates functional osteoclasts, resolving osteopetrosis!).",
