              "rationale": "Neuropathic Osteoarthropathy (Charcot Joint): A severe, progressive, non-infectious, destructive arthropathy occurring in joints deprived of normal pain, temperature, and proprioceptive sensory protective feedback mechanisms. Etiologies: (1) DIABETES MELLITUS WITH SENSORY DIABETIC NEUROPATHY: The LEADING CAUSE OF CHARCOT JOINTS TODAY (> 85-90% of cases!), predominantly affecting the FOOT AND ANKLE: Tarsometatarsal (Lisfranc) joint (45%), Chopart joint, and Ankle; (2) TABES DORSALIS (Tertiary Syphilis): Historically the classic cause, predominantly affecting the KNEE JOINT; (3) SYRINGOMYELIA: Predominantly affects the UPPER EXTREMITY (Shoulder joint in > 80%!); (4) Leprosy (Hansen's disease). Pathophysiology: Loss of protective sensation allows repetitive unperceived microtrauma. Simultaneously, autonomic neuropathy produces continuous sympathetic denervation vasodilation (hyperemic blood flow), stimulating aggressive osteoclastic bone resorption. CLASSICAL RADIOGRAPHIC '6 Ds' OF CHARCOT JOINT (Hypertrophic Pattern): (1) DISTENSION (excessive joint effusion), (2) DISORGANIZATION (loss of normal joint architectural alignment), (3) DISLOCATION / Subluxation of articular surfaces, (4) DEBRIS (massive intra-articular periarticular osseous fragments and loose bodies), (5) DENSITY INCREASE (subchondral osteosclerosis), and (6) DESTRUCTION (resorption and fragmentation of articular bone ends). Classic Clinical Deformity: 'ROCKER-BOTTOM FOOT' (collapse of the tarsometatarsal Lisfranc joints causes the midfoot to sag below the heel and metatarsal heads, producing a convex sole prone to intractable neuropathic plantar ulceration and secondary osteomyelitis). Treatment: Total Contact Casting (TCC) in the acute active inflammatory stage (Eichenholtz Stage 0-1) to immobilize the foot and offload stress until temperature normalizes; custom orthotic footwear (CROW boot).",
