            "question": "A 32-year-old mother of a 2-month-old infant presents with severe radial-sided wrist pain aggravated when lifting her baby. Examination reveals localized tenderness over the radial styloid process. When she flexes her thumb into her palm, wraps her fingers over it to make a fist, and the examiner passively deviates the wrist toward the ulnar side (Finkelstein's Test), she experiences excruciating, sharp pain along the radial styloid. What two tendons within the First Dorsal Extensor Compartment are inflamed?",
