            "topic": "Psoriasis Vulgaris - Auspitz Sign & Histopathology",
            "question": "A 32-year-old male presents with sharply demarcated, erythematous plaques covered by thick, silvery-white micaceous scales on both knees, elbows, and scalp. Gentle scraping of a plaque reveals pinpoint bleeding spots when the last thin scale layer is removed. What is this clinical sign, and what histopathological features are diagnostic?",
