            "topic": "Lichen Planus - The 6 Ps, Wickham's Striae & Civatte Bodies",
            "question": "A 38-year-old female presents with intensely itchy, violaceous, flat-topped polygonal papules on the flexor surfaces of her wrists and shins. Close examination with a magnifying lens reveals a delicate network of lace-like white lines traversing the surface of the lesions (Wickham's Striae). Examination of the oral cavity reveals asymptomatic reticular white streaks on the buccal mucosa. What chronic viral hepatitis infection is epidemiologically associated, and what are the classic histopathological findings?",
