              "rationale": "Systemic Sclerosis (Scleroderma): A systemic autoimmune connective tissue disease characterized by microvascular endothelial damage, immune activation, and widespread excessive deposition of dense collagen in skin and internal organs. TWO MAJOR SUBSETS: (1) LIMITED CUTANEOUS SYSTEMIC SCLEROSIS (lcSSc / CREST SYNDROME): Skin thickening is STRICTLY CONFINED TO AREAS DISTAL TO THE ELBOWS AND KNEES and the FACE/NECK (spares the trunk!). Chronic indolent course; late development of Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension (PAH). CREST ACRONYM: 'C' = CALCINOSIS CUTIS (subcutaneous painful chalky calcium hydroxyapatite deposits over finger pulp and elbows); 'R' = RAYNAUD'S PHENOMENON (triphasic color changes in response to cold: White [ischemia] -> Blue [cyanosis] -> Red [reactive hyperemia]; present in > 95%); 'E' = ESOPHAGEAL DYSMOTILITY (atrophy of smooth muscle in lower 2/3 of esophagus, hypomotility, GERD, Barrett esophagus); 'S' = SCLERODACTYLY (thickening, tightening, and non-pitting induration of skin of fingers; tapering of fingers called 'claw-like / sclerodactyly'); 'T' = TELANGIECTASIA (mat-like dilated post-capillary venules on face, lips, hands). AUTOANTIBODY HALLMARK: ANTI-CENTROMERE ANTIBODIES (ACA / kinetochore pattern on IF; positive in 70-80% of limited SSc, highly specific!); (2) DIFFUSE CUTANEOUS SYSTEMIC SCLEROSIS (dcSSc): Rapidly progressive skin sclerosis involving the TRUNK, ABDOMEN, AND PROXIMAL EXTREMITIES. Early and severe internal organ fibrosis: Interstitial Lung Disease (pulmonary fibrosis: #1 cause of death overall!) and SCLERODERMA RENAL CRISIS (malignant hypertension, microangiopathic hemolytic anemia, acute oliguric renal failure; treated with ACE INHIBITORS [Captopril]!). AUTOANTIBODY HALLMARK: ANTI-SCL-70 (Anti-DNA Topoisomerase I in 30-40%) and Anti-RNA Polymerase III (strongly linked to Scleroderma Renal Crisis). Skin Sign: 'SALT AND PEPPER' PIGMENTATION (leukoderma with sparing of perifollicular pigment).",
