            "topic": "Scabies - Sarcoptes Burrow & Permethrin",
            "question": "A family presents with an epidemic of severe, intractable cutaneous pruritus that characteristically worsens dramatically at night. Physical examination of the parents and children reveals excoriated erythematous papules and delicate, thread-like, serpiginous greyish-white ridges ('Burrows') measuring 5 mm located in the finger web spaces, flexor wrists, axillae, periumbilical area, and genitalia (scrotal nodules). Microscopic scraping of a burrow suspended in mineral oil confirms Sarcoptes scabiei mites, ova, and fecal pellets (Scybala). What is the first-line topical treatment of choice?",
