              "rationale": "Lepra Reactions: Acute inflammatory episodes interrupting the chronic course of leprosy, classified into two major types: (1) TYPE 1 LEPRA REACTION (REVERSAL REACTION): Pathophysiology: TYPE IV (DELAYED-TYPE / CELL-MEDIATED) HYPERSENSITIVITY. Occurs exclusively in borderline forms (BT, BB, BL) with unstable CMI. Driven by an abrupt upgrade (reversal toward TT) or downgrade of CMI against M. leprae antigens. Triggered by initiation of MDT, pregnancy, or intercurrent infection. Clinical Hallmarks: PRE-EXISTING SKIN PATCHES BECOME ACUTELY SWOLLEN, EDEMATOUS, ERYTHEMATOUS, AND WARM (new lesions do NOT appear!); Severe pain and tenderness over peripheral nerves: ACUTE NEURITIS (ulnar, common peroneal, posterior tibial nerves) leading to rapid, irreversible motor paralysis (claw hand, foot drop) and sensory anesthesia. Systemic symptoms (fever) are usually absent or mild. Treatment: HIGH-DOSE ORAL CORTICOSTEROIDS (Prednisone 40-60 mg/day tapered slowly over 3-6 months; prevents permanent nerve damage!). Continue MDT without interruption!; (2) TYPE 2 LEPRA REACTION (ERYTHEMA NODOSUM LEPROSUM / ENL): Pathophysiology: TYPE III (IMMUNE COMPLEX-MEDIATED) ARTHUS-TYPE HYPERSENSITIVITY. Occurs exclusively in multibacillary patients with high bacterial load: LEPROMATOUS LEPROSY (LL) and BORDERLINE LEPROMATOUS (BL). Massive release of bacterial antigens from dying bacilli forms circulating antigen-antibody-complement (C3) immune complexes that deposit in post-capillary venules of skin and internal organs, releasing TNF-alpha. Clinical Hallmarks: Sudden explosive onset of CROPS OF MULTIPLE, PAINFUL, TENDER, ERYTHEMATOUS SUBCUTANEOUS NODULES AND PLAQUES arising on normal-appearing skin (extensor limbs and face), associated with high swinging fever, rigors, severe malaise, bilateral IRIDOCYCLITIS / UVEITIS (risk of blindness!), ORCHITIS / EPIDIDYMO-ORCHITIS (risk of testicular atrophy and sterility!), arthritis, glomerulonephritis, and dactylitis. TREATMENT OF ENL: DRUG OF CHOICE = THALIDOMIDE (100-300 mg daily: potently suppresses TNF-alpha and immune complexes; dramatic relief within 24-48 hours! Strict contraindication: pregnancy due to severe Phocomelia teratogenicity!); Second-line: High-Dose Oral Systemic Corticosteroids (Prednisone) + High-dose CLOFAZIMINE (300 mg daily: has anti-inflammatory action in ENL). Continue MDT!",
