            "question": "A 72-year-old retired farmer presents with multiple rough, sandpaper-like, erythematous, adherent hyperkeratotic papules on the bald scalp and backs of the hands (Actinic Keratoses). Over the lower lip, an indurated, hyperkeratotic, ulcerated, crusted nodule measuring 1.5 cm has developed. Skin biopsy confirms Invasive Squamous Cell Carcinoma. What are the histological hallmarks of well-differentiated Cutaneous SCC?",
