            "question": "A 12-year-old boy presents with an intensely pruritic, boggy, fluctuant, inflammatory, purulent swelling on his scalp with loose hair that easily epilates, accompanied by tender posterior cervical lymphadenopathy (Kerion Celsi). In contrast, another adult patient has expanding annular erythematous plaques with central clearing and an active vesicular border on his trunk (Tinea Corporis). What is the causative fungal pathogen, and what microscopic finding on 10% KOH mount is diagnostic?",
