            "topic": "Genital Ulcers Differential - Chancroid vs LGV vs Donovanosis",
            "question": "A 26-year-old male presents with multiple, exquisitely PAINFUL, soft, non-indurated genital ulcers with ragged undermined borders and a purulent necrotic base on the prepuce, accompanied by a painful, fluctuant, suppurative unilateral inguinal bubo. Gram stain of the purulent exudate demonstrates gram-negative coccobacilli arranged in parallel clusters resembling a 'School of Fish' / 'Railroad Tracks'. What is the causative pathogen, and what features distinguish it from Lymphogranuloma Venereum and Donovanosis?",
