            "question": "A 26-year-old male is brought to the ER unresponsive with pinpoint pupils (miosis), respiratory rate of 4 breaths/minute, cyanosis, and bradycardia. Empty syringes are found in his coat. What is the diagnosis and immediate life-saving antidote?",
