            "question": "A 50-year-old male with an established diagnosis of Schizophrenia presents with mutism, immobility, and remains in bizarre, uncomfortable postures for hours (catalepsy and waxy flexibility). What is the bedside diagnostic challenge test of choice for catatonia?",
