            "id": "RAD_PRAC_U2_01",
            "question_type": "PRACTICE",
            "exam_source": "NEET PG High-Yield Practice (NBE / AIIMS Pattern)",
            "topic": "Intracranial Hemorrhages - EDH vs SDH vs SAH",
            "question": "A 22-year-old motorcyclist sustains head trauma with brief loss of consciousness, followed by a 2-hour 'lucid interval', then rapid coma and an ipsilateral dilated, fixed pupil. Non-contrast brain CT reveals a hyperdense, biconvex (lenticular) extra-axial collection that does not cross cranial suture lines. What is the diagnosis and injured vessel?",
