              "rationale": "The ASA Physical Status classification grades perioperative systemic health: ASA I = Normal healthy patient; ASA II = Mild systemic disease without functional limitations (e.g. well-controlled hypertension, mild asthma); ASA III = Severe systemic disease that results in substantive functional limitations (e.g. COPD with limitation, stable angina, EF 35%); ASA IV = Severe systemic disease that is a constant threat to life (e.g. unstable angina, ongoing sepsis, end-stage renal disease without dialysis); ASA V = Moribund patient not expected to survive 24 hours without surgery; ASA VI = Brain-dead organ donor. The suffix 'E' denotes emergency surgery.",
