            "question": "A firefighter rescued from a burning apartment building presents with confusion, cherry-red skin, and burns. Arterial blood gas co-oximetry confirms a carboxyhemoglobin (CO-Hb) level of 38%. What will the standard dual-wavelength operating room pulse oximeter (SpO2) display, and why?",
