            "question": "A 28-year-old female non-smoker with a history of motion sickness undergoes laparoscopic cholecystectomy under general anesthesia with Sevoflurane and postoperative IV Morphine. According to the Apfel simplified risk score, how many risk factors for Postoperative Nausea and Vomiting (PONV) does she possess, and what is her predicted PONV risk?",
